From a615561cd81946a779d7a613da0de094af6ee023 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter0x44 <peter0x44@disroot.org>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 00:20:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: Handle diagnostic colors on Windows consoles

Ccache forces supported compilers to produce colored diagnostics because their output is captured instead of written directly to the terminal. It later decides whether to strip the resulting ANSI sequences before replaying the diagnostics.

On Windows, consider automatic color available only for a native console handle, independently of TERM. Try to enable virtual terminal processing as GCC does. If VT remains unavailable, translate supported SGR and erase-line sequences to Win32 console operations so legacy consoles retain readable colored diagnostics.

Keep redirected output unchanged and avoid changing console modes for compilers that do not support forced diagnostic colors. The translation is based on GCC's MinGW console handling in gcc/pretty-print.cc.
